# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Python
__pycache__/

# Node (if any tooling is added later)
node_modules/

# Smart Web Search cache (per-project, generated at runtime)
.smart-search-cache/

# Antigravity CLI (agy) per-project tracking — runtime state, created when agy
# touches the project. Symlinks into ~/.gemini/config/projects/<UUID>.json.
.antigravitycli/

# Commit-gate review attestation (per-project runtime state). Written by the
# /commit skill's gate (`evolve commit-gate run`, go/internal/commitgate/) and
# verified at the commit chokepoint (`evolve ship --class manual`). Never
# committed — it binds to the local tree SHA.
.commit-gate/

# Evolve Loop runtime state (generated per-project, not part of the plugin)
# Ignore every direct child of .evolve/ ...
# v8.21.0+: per-cycle git worktrees live at .evolve/worktrees/cycle-N — also
# implicitly ignored by this rule. Worktrees are created by run-cycle.sh
# and removed via its EXIT trap; they should never appear in commits.
.evolve/*
# Nested .evolve dirs only (e.g. runtime state created inside per-cycle
# worktrees). v16.6 operator fix: was `**/.evolve/`, which also matched the
# ROOT .evolve/ directory and dead-lettered every whitelist below (a directory
# exclusion forbids re-including descendants) — new phase.json/agent.md/
# profile files could only be staged with `git add -f`. Root .evolve/ is
# governed by the `.evolve/*` ladder above + the explicit re-includes below.
*/**/.evolve/
# ... except the agent permission profiles, which ship with the plugin and are
# required by scripts/subagent-run.sh for least-privilege subagent invocation.
!.evolve/profiles/
.evolve/profiles/*
!.evolve/profiles/*.json
!.evolve/profiles/*.md
# ... but runtime-minted profile STUBS (empty cli, no persona pairing) must NOT ride
# into tracking: TestSmoke_RealProfiles + TestRepoPersonaProfilePairing validate every
# tracked profile, and the v22.13.0 release burned on exactly this (2026-08-04; same
# class as the gate-wiring-proof stubs below). Dispatch reads them from DISK — leave
# the files in place, just never track them until they satisfy the repo contracts.
.evolve/profiles/ship-stage-hygiene-check.json
.evolve/profiles/regression-predicate-precheck.json
.evolve/profiles/ci-parity-preflight.json
# ... and except the directory marker for failure-lessons. Generated lesson
# YAMLs (inst-L*.yaml) are per-project runtime state and remain ignored, but
# the .keep marker ships so the directory exists in fresh installs.
!.evolve/instincts/
.evolve/instincts/*
!.evolve/instincts/lessons/
.evolve/instincts/lessons/*
!.evolve/instincts/lessons/.keep
# ... and except the inbox API directory. Operator-injected task files in the root
# of inbox/ are tracked; processed/, processing/ and rejected/ are runtime subdirs
# (gitignored).
!.evolve/inbox/
.evolve/inbox/processed/
.evolve/inbox/processing/
.evolve/inbox/rejected/
# ... and except the subagent-skills plugin directory. Loaded by Builder/Auditor
# subagents via --plugin-dir to make review skills (code-review-simplify,
# security-review-scored) resolvable under --setting-sources project. Manifest
# is tracked; skills/ entries are symlinks to .agents/skills/ (also tracked).
!.evolve/plugin/
!.evolve/plugin/.claude-plugin/
!.evolve/plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
!.evolve/plugin/skills/
!.evolve/plugin/skills/*
# ... and except the Layer 1 (ADR-0012) commit-prefix manifest. Defines what
# commit prefixes (docs:, feat(guards):, etc.) require which diff paths.
# Operator-extensible but ships with sensible defaults; must be tracked so the
# scripts/guards/commit-prefix-gate.sh hook applies consistently across clones.
!.evolve/commit-prefix-scope.json
# ... and except the operator policy file (ADR-0055 D3). Defines floor gates
# (e.g. dossier-closeout) that must pass before a cycle can ship. Operator-
# extensible; must be tracked so the gate applies consistently across clones.
!.evolve/policy.json
# ... and except the naming-guard manifest (SSOT for the legacynames acs gate,
# `evolve release` preflight, and `evolve names`). Lists the dead naming tokens a
# rename leaves behind; must be tracked so the guard applies across all clones.
!.evolve/naming.json
# ... and except user-defined phase specs. Operators drop a phase.json under
# .evolve/phases/<name>/phase.json to extend the pipeline declaratively.
# Analogous to .evolve/profiles/ — must be tracked so new phases ship with the
# project and survive clone. (recoverBuildLeak already skips .evolve/ paths, so
# tracking these files does not re-introduce the cycle-176 incident.)
!.evolve/phases/
.evolve/phases/*
!.evolve/phases/*/
.evolve/phases/*/*
!.evolve/phases/*/phase.json
# v16.6 (cycle-217 operator fix): agent personas authored beside the spec
# (ADR-0035 authoring path: .evolve/phases/<name>/agent.md) must ship too —
# without this line, ship's plain `git add -A` silently drops them.
!.evolve/phases/*/agent.md
# ... and except the EGPS eval definitions. The tracked eval corpus has existed
# since 2026-06-01 and eval-materialization lanes DELIVER new evals — but this
# re-include was missing, so every new eval was born ignored: check-ignore could
# not flag the pathspec (tracked content exempts the dir), ship staging kept it,
# and `git add` refused the whole .evolve/evals pathspec (rc=1) — the
# cycle-1345/1346/1348 identical-fingerprint batch HALT (2026-08-05). Scoped to
# *.md, mirroring the phases/profiles ladder idiom.
!.evolve/evals/
.evolve/evals/*
!.evolve/evals/*.md
# NOTE (issue-#11 / cycle-176, updated 2026-08-05): a self-evolve cycle (ee77067)
# un-ignored .evolve/ WHOLESALE (`!.evolve/`) to "track evals". That broke a
# then-LOAD-BEARING invariant — recoverBuildLeak and the audit assumed .evolve/
# fully gitignored — and was reverted, with the note that versioning evals needs
# a deliberate redesign, not a blanket un-ignore. That redesign has since
# happened piecemeal: leak recovery gives .evolve/evals and .evolve/phases
# DELIBERATE per-prefix handling (core/leak_recovery.go evolveDeliverablePrefixes)
# while the generic .evolve/ skip covers the rest; ship staging drops ignored
# declared paths (dropIgnoredPaths); and eval-quality gates validate eval
# content. The scoped `.evolve/evals/*.md` ladder above is the missing final
# piece — the tracked corpus the revert left in place is now consistent with
# the ignore rules. Blanket `!.evolve/` remains forbidden; the birth-coherence
# pin (go/internal/phasecoherence/gitignore_birth_test.go) now enforces
# corpus↔ladder consistency both ways.
.claude/evolve/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# Campaign/dev git worktrees (e.g. .worktrees/modularize-unify-phaseio) — isolated
# checkouts of this repo created via `git worktree add .worktrees/<name>`. Never
# part of the tracked tree; ignored so the parent worktree's `git status` stays clean.
.worktrees/
.clone/
.ruff_cache/
*.pyc

# Cycle 65 incident: prevent stderr-redirected warnings from being committed.
# role-context-builder.sh anchor-validation can emit a stderr WARN that
# Orchestrator captures as `warn.txt` at repo root. ship.sh `git add -A`
# would then sweep it into the cycle commit (causes audit-bound tree-SHA
# drift; see docs/incidents/cycle-65-warn-txt.md if/when authored).
/warn.txt
*.warn
parity-audit-report.md

# Phase-report runtime artifacts. Agents write these to their cwd (a per-cycle
# worktree = a checkout of this repo), and the builder's `git add -A` + worktree
# commit will sweep them into the repo root if they aren't ignored — that is how
# a stale `build-report.md` (Cycle 65, 27bee92) ended up tracked and got
# relocated into cycle-145 by artifactReady's worktree search (audit FAIL on a
# wrong challenge token). These belong only under .evolve/runs/cycle-N/.
build-report.md
scout-report.md
audit-report.md
triage-report.md
test-report.md
build-plan.md
*-reflection.yaml

# Go coverage artifacts (`go test -coverprofile`). Never commit: left untracked
# they get swept into cycle commits by `git add -A` and drift the committed tree
# from the audit-bound tree (INTEGRITY_TREE_DRIFT, cycle-152).
cover.out
coverage.out
*.coverprofile

# Boot-smoke / bridge log dropped in the repo root by `evolve release` preflight.
# Never commit: it was swept into the v18.3.0 release commit by the broad stage.
evolve*.log
release-*.log
routing-plan.json

# campaign run logs (per-run runtime artifact)
campaign.log

# goreleaser local snapshot output (release runs in CI)
/dist/

# Stray compiled `evolve` executables an ACS predicate's `go build <main pkg>`
# left in its package dir (tracked-binary-in-acs-dir: an 18MB go/acs/cycle536/evolve
# was committed this way). The build predicates now use `-o os.DevNull`; this is
# belt-and-suspenders so a regression can never be `git add`ed again.
go/acs/**/evolve

# Runtime-minted per-host phase stubs (ADR-0074 wired no-op): dispatch reads them
# from DISK; tracking them fails phasecoherence (profile with no persona) and
# phasespec (no SELECT metadata). Ship's staging sweep must never re-add them.
.evolve/phases/gate-wiring-proof/
.evolve/profiles/gate-wiring-proof.json
